Fn symbols: Fn+D and Fn+' are not also Alt; Fn+R/Fn+T match the keycaps

The input daemon (funkeymonkey-pyrainput) makes the Fn layer by sending
spare keycodes, and this file gives them their symbols. Two of them are
wrong in 0.39:

- Fn+D (KEY 197, <META>) and Fn+' (KEY 196, <ALT>) type `_` and `:`, but
  the pc symbols give both codes Mod1 and Alt_L/Meta_L on level 2, and this
  file adds `modifier_map Mod1 { <META> }`. XKB's catch-all interpretation
  then makes each key an Alt modifier while it is down. A key pressed before
  `_` or `:` is released arrives as Alt+key (xterm types `â` for b,
  mate-terminal sends ESC b, which moves bash back a word), and Shift+Fn+D or
  Shift+Fn+' types nothing. Both levels now hold the symbol and the key has
  an explicit NoAction(), which wins over the interpretation.
- Fn+R types è and Fn+T types é; the keycaps print é on R and è on T.

Checked 2026-11-21 on the trixie card by injecting the keycodes through
uinput into xterm and mate-terminal (development log, R78).

Against pyra-config-xorg 0.39 (/usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/pyra; 0.38 has the
same file).

--- a/usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/pyra
+++ b/usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/pyra
